      "Mercy is what God shows when He encounters those who deserve His judgement and chooses, instead, to forgive, restore, and bless. It is one of the most frequently named attributes in Scripture, and one of the most surprising. The God we have been describing as holy, sovereign, and wise is, in His own self-revelation, also overflowing with mercy. 'The Lord, the Lord, a God merciful and gracious, slow to anger, abounding in steadfast love and faithfulness' (Ex 34:6) is the self-description God gives Moses in the most defining theophany of the Old Testament.",
      "Notice three things about God's mercy. First, it is not reluctance. God does not extend mercy because His justice was overruled or because we wore Him down. He delights in mercy. Micah 7:18 says of Him, 'He delights in steadfast love.' Mercy flows from who He is, not from what we have managed to extract from Him.",
